# Uroboros settings: every environment variable it reads, and the setups that use them.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      (.env is gitignored)
#
# Docker Compose reads `.env` from the repository root on every `docker compose` command, the
# `mise run docker:*` tasks included, and substitutes it into compose.yaml. A variable set in your
# shell wins over the file. Every line here is commented out, so a fresh copy changes nothing:
# uncomment what you change. The value after `=` is what you get with the line left commented.
#
# Each variable says who reads it:
#   [compose]  compose hands it to the server from this file.
#   [fixed]    compose or the image sets it itself, so it only matters for a server you run
#              yourself: `mise run dev:server`, `docker run --env-file`, Kubernetes and so on.
#              mise doesn't read this file; load it first with `set -a && . ./.env && set +a`.
#   [host]     compose itself (a host port, a GPU overlay), not the server.
#
# The server refuses a bad value at startup (exit 2) and treats an empty optional one as unset.
# README's Configuration table has the same list; docs/ has the designs behind it. Quote a value
# with spaces in single quotes: compose and the shell strip them, `docker run --env-file` doesn't.
#
# ── Setups ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. The local stack, transcoding on the CPU. Nothing to set.
#      mise run docker:up        the production image on http://127.0.0.1:18080 (loopback only)
#      mise run docker:up:dev    server and UI hot-reloading from source, port 18080 on every
#                                interface, Postgres and RustFS on loopback ports
#      mise run docker:down      stops either
#    Both run one uroboros behind Caddy; `docker compose up --scale uroboros=2` runs more, which
#    share the work. Sign in as admin / admin, a dev-only account (see Sign-in below). The
#    docker:* tasks need `docker login code.example.com` first, for the ffmpeg image.
#
# 2. Transcoding on an NVIDIA GPU (NVENC). Install the NVIDIA driver and the NVIDIA Container
#    Toolkit, and generate its CDI spec once:
#      sudo nvidia-ctk cdi generate --output=/etc/cdi/nvidia.yaml
#    Then add compose/gpu/nvidia.yaml, which passes the GPU in and sets
#    UROBOROS_TRANSCODE_HWACCEL=nvenc:
#      COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose/gpu/nvidia.yaml        (below, for `mise run docker:up`)
#      docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.dev.yaml -f compose/gpu/nvidia.yaml up
#                                                                (the dev stack)
#
# 3. Transcoding on an AMD GPU (VA-API; Intel untested). The container needs the render node and
#    the host's render group:
#      getent group render | cut -d: -f3       the group id, for UROBOROS_RENDER_GID (below)
#      ls /dev/dri/                            renderD128 is the first GPU; another one goes in
#                                              UROBOROS_TRANSCODE_VAAPI_DEVICE
#    Then add compose/gpu/vaapi.yaml, which sets UROBOROS_TRANSCODE_HWACCEL=vaapi:
#      COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose/gpu/vaapi.yaml
#      docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.dev.yaml -f compose/gpu/vaapi.yaml up
#
#    With either GPU the server tests it at startup and logs "transcoding on the GPU", or warns
#    "the GPU can't encode; transcoding on the CPU instead". The line under the player names the
#    encoder ("Transcoding to 720p · NVIDIA GPU"). Videos the browser plays never transcode
#    (docs/transcoding.md).
#
# 4. Organized folders instead of S3: UROBOROS_STORAGE=filesystem. Compose keeps them on the
#    media-data volume at /media; mount a host folder there in a compose override to see them.
#
# 5. A server run on the host, with no container for it:
#      mise run dev:deps          Postgres :15432 and RustFS :19000
#      mise run dev:server        the server on http://127.0.0.1:18081
#      mise run dev:ui            Vite on http://127.0.0.1:18173
#    Their defaults point at dev:deps, so nothing needs setting. It downloads and transcodes with
#    yt-dlp and ffmpeg from PATH (jellyfin-ffmpeg is in the image only).
#
# 6. Facing other people: put an https proxy in front and set UROBOROS_PUBLIC_BASE_URL (push and
#    SSO need it); replace the admin / admin account (your own bootstrap admin with
#    UROBOROS_ALLOW_WEAK_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=false, or SSO with UROBOROS_LOCAL_LOGIN=false); set a
#    UROBOROS_SECRETS_KEY and keep it. Postgres and RustFS have fixed dev credentials in
#    compose.yaml: change them there first.

# ── Compose and host ports [host] ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The compose files, `:`-separated, for `docker compose` and `mise run docker:up`. A command's own
# -f flags win, and the docker:up:dev tasks pass theirs, so add an overlay to the dev stack with
# -f (setups 2 and 3).
# COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml

# Caddy's port: loopback in compose.yaml, every interface in the dev stack.
# UROBOROS_PORT=18080

# The dev stack's loopback ports, which `mise run dev:deps` uses too. A host-run server also needs
# DATABASE_URL or UROBOROS_S3_ENDPOINT moved to match.
# UROBOROS_POSTGRES_PORT=15432
# UROBOROS_S3_PORT=19000
# UROBOROS_S3_CONSOLE_PORT=19001

# The host's render group id, required by compose/gpu/vaapi.yaml (setup 3).
# UROBOROS_RENDER_GID=

# ── Server and database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [fixed] Required. Postgres; compose uses postgres://uroboros:uroboros@postgres:5432/uroboros.
# Also read by `mise run migrate`.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://uroboros:uroboros@127.0.0.1:15432/uroboros

# [fixed] host:port to listen on; the image sets 0.0.0.0:8080.
# UROBOROS_BIND=127.0.0.1:18081

# [fixed] The built SPA to serve (unset: none); the image sets /app/web.
# UROBOROS_WEB_DIST=

# [fixed] The SQL migrations (unset: the repo's migrations/); the image sets /app/migrations.
# Every replica applies pending ones as it starts.
# UROBOROS_MIGRATIONS_DIR=

# [fixed] Read the client IP from X-Forwarded-For, for the per-IP sign-in limit. Compose sets
# true (Caddy is in front); set it behind any proxy.
# UROBOROS_TRUST_PROXY=false

# [compose] How long startup retries an unreachable Postgres before exiting 1, in seconds
# (0: until it answers).
# UROBOROS_DB_STARTUP_GRACE_SECS=0

# [compose] After SIGTERM, how long in-flight requests may run, in ms. Running downloads get 25 s,
# then go back to the queue.
# UROBOROS_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS=20000

# [compose] The largest request body /api/* accepts, in bytes; larger gets 413.
# UROBOROS_BODY_LIMIT_BYTES=65536

# ── Storage (docs/downloads.md) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [compose] Where media goes: s3, or filesystem (organized folders). Required outside compose.
# UROBOROS_STORAGE=s3

# [fixed] For s3: the endpoint and an existing bucket. Compose uses its RustFS at
# http://rustfs:9000, whose rustfs-init creates the bucket.
# UROBOROS_S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:19000
# UROBOROS_S3_BUCKET=uroboros

# [fixed] For s3: the access key pair; compose's are RustFS's dev ones.
# UROBOROS_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=uroboros
# UROBOROS_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=uroboros-dev-secret

# [compose] For s3: the region.
# UROBOROS_S3_REGION=us-east-1

# [fixed] For s3: path-style addressing (RustFS and MinIO-style servers need it).
# UROBOROS_S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true

# [compose] For s3: an endpoint browsers can reach. Set, "save file" redirects to a presigned URL
# there; unset, files stream through the server.
# UROBOROS_S3_PUBLIC_URL=

# [fixed] For filesystem: the absolute path of the media folder every replica shares; compose
# uses /media (the media-data volume).
# UROBOROS_STORAGE_ROOT=

# [compose] For filesystem: the folder layout. Tokens: channel, uploader, title, id, extractor,
# upload_date, year, profile, ext; a custom layout must use {id}, {profile} and {ext}.
# UROBOROS_STORAGE_LAYOUT='{channel}/{upload_date} {title} [{id}]/{title} [{profile}].{ext}'

# ── Downloads and subscriptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [compose] Download jobs each replica runs at once.
# UROBOROS_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=4

# [compose] Downloads of one person running at once; the rest wait their turn.
# UROBOROS_MAX_ACTIVE_DOWNLOADS_PER_USER=3

# [compose] Entries kept per playlist or channel-tab preview.
# UROBOROS_MAX_PLAYLIST_ENTRIES=1000

# [compose] The shortest check interval a subscription may have, in minutes.
# UROBOROS_MIN_CHECK_INTERVAL_MINUTES=60

# [compose] The largest video a person may upload, in bytes (10 GiB; at most 80 GiB). Uploads go in
# 8 MiB parts, so a reverse proxy in front must take request bodies of 8 MiB (docs/uploads.md).
# UROBOROS_UPLOAD_MAX_BYTES=10737418240

# [compose] Subtitles saved with each download (yt-dlp --sub-langs), and whether automatic
# captions count. An uncommented empty UROBOROS_SUBTITLE_LANGS= saves none.
# UROBOROS_SUBTITLE_LANGS=en.*
# UROBOROS_AUTO_SUBTITLES=false

# [compose] 32 random bytes in base64 (openssl rand -base64 32) sealing people's saved site logins
# (Settings › Logins). Unset, saving logins is off; a new key voids the saved ones. The dev stack
# has a fixed dev key; never reuse it.
# UROBOROS_SECRETS_KEY=

# [fixed] Scratch space for downloads in progress (unset: $TMPDIR/uroboros-work); compose uses a
# tmpfs at /work.
# UROBOROS_WORK_DIR=

# [fixed] The yt-dlp binary (unset: yt-dlp on PATH); the image sets /opt/yt-dlp/bin/yt-dlp.
# YTDLP_PATH=

# ── Transcoding (docs/transcoding.md) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Videos the browser can play are played as they are. The others, and any lower quality a viewer
# picks, play through a session that remuxes or transcodes on the fly (setups 2 and 3 for a GPU).

# [compose] Playback sessions each replica runs at once; 0 runs none there. A paused viewer holds
# one while their tab is open, but costs nothing.
# UROBOROS_TRANSCODE_CONCURRENCY=2

# [compose] The replica's GPU: none (the CPU, libx264), nvenc (NVIDIA) or vaapi (AMD). The GPU
# overlays set it, together with the device it needs; set alone, the GPU test fails and the CPU
# transcodes. A failing pipeline falls back to CPU decoding, then to the CPU.
# UROBOROS_TRANSCODE_HWACCEL=none

# [compose] The VA-API render node, with vaapi; compose/gpu/vaapi.yaml passes this node in.
# UROBOROS_TRANSCODE_VAAPI_DEVICE=/dev/dri/renderD128

# [compose] Hover previews (docs/library.md): each video gets a short silent 480p clip of snippets
# from across it, cut on the CPU by replicas that run sessions; videos already stored get theirs
# in the background. false makes none, new or old; the ones already made still play.
# UROBOROS_GENERATE_PREVIEWS=true

# ── Sign-in (docs/auth.md) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [compose] How long a session lasts, in hours.
# UROBOROS_SESSION_TTL_HOURS=720

# [compose] Username and password sign-in. Off, OIDC must be configured.
# UROBOROS_LOCAL_LOGIN=true

# [compose] An admin re-seeded on every start; both or neither, the password 12+ characters.
# Compose defaults to admin / admin and allows the weak password; outside compose there is none.
# UROBOROS_BOOTSTRAP_USERNAME=admin
# UROBOROS_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=admin

# [compose] Accept a bootstrap password under 12 characters (logs a warning). Compose sets true for
# its dev account; the server's own default is false. Never true for real use.
# UROBOROS_ALLOW_WEAK_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=true

# [compose] SSO through an OIDC provider: all three or none, and an https UROBOROS_PUBLIC_BASE_URL
# for the callback (<base>/api/auth/oidc/callback). An SSO user's role comes from their groups.
# UROBOROS_OIDC_ISSUER=
# UROBOROS_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# UROBOROS_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=

# [compose] The provider's name on the sign-in button, the groups whose members are admins
# (comma-separated), and the ID-token claim holding the groups.
# UROBOROS_OIDC_DISPLAY_NAME=Authentik
# UROBOROS_OIDC_ADMIN_GROUPS='authentik Admins'
# UROBOROS_OIDC_GROUPS_CLAIM=groups

# [compose] How stale SSO claims may get before they are refreshed, in seconds; 0 turns it off.
# UROBOROS_OIDC_SYNC_INTERVAL_SECS=900

# ── Install and push notifications (docs/push.md) ───────────────────────────────────────────────

# [compose] The public origin, no path (https://uroboros.example.com). Push is on only when it is
# https.
# UROBOROS_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# [compose] The VAPID contact, a mailto: address or an https URL (unset: the public URL).
# UROBOROS_PUSH_SUBJECT=

# [compose] A fixed VAPID key pair, both or neither. Unset, the first replica generates one and
# keeps it in the database. Changing it drops every device's subscription.
# UROBOROS_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# UROBOROS_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=

# [compose] Hosts a push endpoint may be on, or a subdomain of, comma-separated (unset: Apple,
# Google, Mozilla and Microsoft push).
# UROBOROS_PUSH_ALLOWED_HOSTS=push.apple.com,fcm.googleapis.com,push.services.mozilla.com,notify.windows.com

# [compose] Devices with notifications per person.
# UROBOROS_PUSH_MAX_DEVICES=10

# ── Development and tests [fixed] ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `mise run dev:ui`: where Vite proxies /api, and its own port.
# UROBOROS_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18081
# UROBOROS_UI_PORT=18173

# `mise run test`: an existing Postgres and RustFS to use instead of starting containers
# (unset: testcontainers). Two runs must not share one Postgres at once; RustFS must use the
# credentials in apps/server/test/s3Credentials.ts.
# UROBOROS_TEST_DATABASE_URL=
# UROBOROS_TEST_S3_URL=
